⍝ UCI engine: reads commands from stdin and writes replies to stdout.
⍝
⍝ Usage: dyalogscript uci.apls

⎕IO ⎕ML←1

SOURCE_TYPES←'.apln' '.aplc' '.apli' '.aplf' '.aplo'

findFiles←{{⍵[⍋⍵]}⊆⊃0(⎕NINFO⍠1)⍵}

isSourceFile←{(⊂3⊃1 ⎕NPARTS ⍵)∊SOURCE_TYPES}

⍝ Each reply line is terminated by a newline; no replies writes nothing.
writeLines←{('UTF-8'⎕UCS∊⍵,¨⎕UCS 10)⎕NAPPEND stdout 83}

⍝ End of input means the GUI has gone away, which is treated as quit.
readLine←{1005::UCI.CMD_QUIT ⋄ ⍞}

args←2 ⎕NQ'.' 'GetCommandLineArgs'
root←⊃1 ⎕NPARTS⊃args
paths←findFiles root,'APLSource/*'
_←{2 ⎕FIX'file://',⍵}¨(isSourceFile¨paths)/paths

⍝ Under dyalogscript, ⍞← writes to stderr and ⎕← ends lines with a
⍝ carriage return. UCI GUIs read newline-terminated lines from stdout,
⍝ so replies are written to the stdout file descriptor directly.
⍝ It is tied write-only: when stdout is a pipe, macOS refuses to open
⍝ /dev/stdout for reading and writing, which is ⎕NTIE's default.
stdout←'/dev/stdout'⎕NTIE 0 1

state←UCI.newState LookupTables.createLookupTables ⍬
:Repeat
    (state replies)←state UCI.handle readLine ⍬
    _←writeLines replies
:Until UCI.finished state

⎕OFF
